Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: a plain IEEE 1905 Topology Response leaves the backhaul station rows

0047 answers a neighbor-only Topology Notification with a Topology Query to each agent (the
liveness probe). An agent's IEEE 1905 layer answers it with a plain Topology Response: Device
Information and its neighbors, no EasyMesh TLV. handle_topology_response rejects such a response
("topology response msg validation failed, ignoring message"), but only after its Device
Information slice (0216, 0248, 0254) has run, and that slice takes any response without RDK's
vendor operational BSS snapshot for an adapter's: a backhaul station row whose station the
response does not list connected is counted, and removed at the second such response. A plain
response lists no station connected, so every RDK agent's link row (its station's row on its
radio, from the vendor snapshot: its parent's BSSID, or zero when wired) went at the second probe
answer and came back with the agent's next EasyMesh response.
Seen on rdk-1010 (16 October, steady state, no room running): one probe burst's plain answers
at 17:22:42Z removed four link rows from the database within a second (the gateway's and the
wired extender's zero-BSSID rows, two extenders' rows to their parents; BSSList 72, 70, then 68
rows), and the agents' next EasyMesh responses wrote them back ten seconds later. Such bursts
came every 7 to 14 minutes. An RDK agent's EasyMesh response does not end a row's count, so a
count one burst left removed the row at the next burst's first answer. In rooms rounds, where
neighbors change more often, the model was short of link rows about ten times a round, link
rows only (14 and 16 October).

The slice now runs only for a response with the AP Operational BSS TLV, the response the handler
goes on to accept: a plain response learns, moves and removes no station row, nor counts toward a
removal. An adapter's EasyMesh responses (EMOSA always sends the TLV) keep 0254's rule as it was.
gen/tests/controller-learned-station-rows-test.py: --expect-dropped reproduces the dropped link
rows, connected and wired, on 0001-0268; on 0001-0269 they stay, plain responses neither learn,
move, remove nor count a pod's learned row, and two EasyMesh responses with no station connected
still remove it.

Platform-independent.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
--- a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
+++ b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
@@ -2921,6 +2921,12 @@ int em_configuration_t::handle_topology_response(unsigned char *buff, unsigned i
      * models no radio for it) and removed when the interface is no longer
      * reported. */
     bool vendor_bss_snapshot = false;
+    /* A response without the AP Operational BSS TLV is a plain IEEE 1905 one:
+     * an agent's 1905 layer answering the controller's liveness query (0047).
+     * It reports no EasyMesh BSS, lists no backhaul station connected, and is
+     * rejected below; its Device Information learns, moves and removes no
+     * backhaul station's row either, nor counts toward a row's removal. */
+    bool operational_bss = false;
     {
         unsigned char *scan = device_cursor;
         unsigned int scan_remaining = device_remaining;
@@ -2932,7 +2938,8 @@ int em_configuration_t::handle_topology_response(unsigned char *buff, unsigned i
             }
             if (scan_tlv->type == em_tlv_type_vendor_operational_bss) {
                 vendor_bss_snapshot = true;
-                break;
+            } else if (scan_tlv->type == em_tlv_type_operational_bss) {
+                operational_bss = true;
             }
             scan += scan_total;
             scan_remaining -= scan_total;
@@ -2941,7 +2948,7 @@ int em_configuration_t::handle_topology_response(unsigned char *buff, unsigned i
     /* the station interfaces this response reports, each with its network membership */
     mac_address_t reported_bsta[EM_MAX_BSSS];
     unsigned int num_reported_bsta = 0;
-    while (device_remaining >= sizeof(em_tlv_t)) {
+    while (operational_bss && device_remaining >= sizeof(em_tlv_t)) {
         em_tlv_t *device_tlv = reinterpret_cast<em_tlv_t *>(device_cursor);
         unsigned int value_len = ntohs(device_tlv->len);
         unsigned int total_len = sizeof(em_tlv_t) + value_len;
@@ -3164,7 +3171,7 @@ int em_configuration_t::handle_topology_response(unsigned char *buff, unsigned i
         device_cursor += total_len;
         device_remaining -= total_len;
     }
-    if (!vendor_bss_snapshot) {
+    if (operational_bss && !vendor_bss_snapshot) {
         for (int index = static_cast<int>(dm->get_num_bss()) - 1; index >= 0; index--) {
             em_bss_info_t *row = dm->get_bss_info(static_cast<unsigned int>(index));
             /* Such a station's row: a backhaul row in station mode, or one
